# Alternate pronunciations (multiple variants) not collapsed

## ==Original Issue==

I've run a test:
python -m edgepron.cli --vital-level 4 --popular-limit 500 --condensed output-v4-p500-oct24-938am.tsv
that output is in the resources directory.
Many of the pronunciations have alternate versions, separated by commas. My
presumptive solution: truncate at the first comma and keep only the first
variant. For the condensed lookup we want exactly ONE pairing per headword.

### Concrete examples
- `Marcello Mastroianni` -> `mar-CHEL-oh-_-MA(H)ST-roh-YA(H)N-ee-,_-_-MA(H)ST-roy-AH-nee`
- `Michelangelo`          -> alternates separated by `,_`
- `Vladimir Nabokov`      -> alternates
- `Kurt Lewin`            -> alternates

## Investigation notes (agent)
The alternates live in the *native* `{{respell}}` output. `normalize_respell`
joins syllables with `-`, and a template param like `,_-_` becomes the literal
`,`, so the comma survives into the final string. The IPA-derived path already
truncates at the first comma (see `_ipa_to_respell`: `ipa.replace("_","
").split(",")[0]`), but the native-respell path does NOT — that asymmetry is
the bug.

## ==Status Report: 2026-10-24 18:10 US/Pacific==

Implemented. `normalize_respell` now splits the joined syllable string at the
first `,` and strips trailing `_`/`-`/whitespace, so only the first variant is
kept (the IPA-derived path already truncated at the comma in `_ipa_to_respell`).
Live-checked against the real "Marcello Mastroianni" lead:
`mar-CHEL-oh-_-MA(H)ST-roh-YA(H)N-ee` (alternates dropped). Added
`test_respell_alternates_are_truncated_at_comma`. Full suite: 174 passed.
